/*
 * Real artwork for the "Third Party / Developer" icons whose own artwork the Lucid export lost.
 *
 * `scripts/convert_lucid_shapes.py` can only draw what the .lcsl gives it a vector path for. These
 * icons carried their logo as a bitmap (`UserImage2Block`), or as a glyph filled with the same
 * off-white as the tile behind it, so in the palette they were an empty rounded square. Each entry
 * here replaces everything after the tile's own background (path 0) with a logo drawn in its own box.
 *
 * Sourced from the SVG Logos collection (`@iconify-json/logos`, CC0) and Simple Icons (CC0) -- only the
 * path data and brand colours were taken, nothing is loaded at runtime. `microsoft-teams` and
 * `servicenow` have no usable source and are a plain stand-in mark (a "T" tile, a ring) rather than the
 * official logo. Trademarks remain their owners'.
 *
 * `width`/`height` are the logo's own coordinate box; `LucidArt` scales it to fit inside the tile.
 * To change one, edit it here -- `lucid.json` is generated and a re-run would not carry it.
 */
